# This project is built into a Linux Docker image and run there. Files consumed
# by s6-overlay, the shell, and nginx MUST use LF. On Windows (core.autocrlf) a
# checkout or `git archive` would otherwise write CRLF, which breaks
# `s6-rc-compile` at container boot:
#   fatal: invalid /etc/s6-overlay/s6-rc.d/<svc>/type: must be oneshot, longrun, or bundle
# Pinning eol=lf here keeps rebuilds safe regardless of the builder's platform.
docker/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
